---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms under which this site is published, what its calculators do and do not cover, and the limits of what it can promise."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-head">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Terms</span>
      </nav>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">
        Plain terms for a site that publishes calculations rather than
        recommendations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What this site provides</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} publishes calculators and written explanations of the
        arithmetic behind them. The calculators apply published formulas to
        values you supply and return the result together with the working.
        That is the whole service.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site does not provide</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing here is financial, tax, legal or investment advice, and nothing
        here is a recommendation to buy, sell, hold, rent, own, refinance or
        sign anything. A result reflects the inputs you entered and the
        formula on the page. Change an input and the result changes; that is
        what makes it a calculation rather than a conclusion.
      </p>
      <p>
        A calculator cannot see your finances, your income, your credit, your
        time horizon or your risk tolerance, and it does not try to guess at
        them. Two people with the same inputs and different circumstances will
        reach different conclusions, and the calculator is not in a position
        to say which of them is right.
      </p>

      <h2>Figures, sources and dates</h2>
      <p>
        Where a figure comes from an outside source, the page links to that
        source and gives the date it was read. Outside data changes: tax
        thresholds, published rates and official statistics are all revised.
        A figure on a page is accurate as of the review date on that page and
        no longer, and the review date is there so you can see how old it is.
      </p>

      <h2>Errors</h2>
      <p>
        The calculations are implemented once, in one place, and tested. Even
        so, a mistake is possible. If you find one, the
        <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> explains how to report it, and
        reported defects are fixed and the review date updated.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The site is funded by display advertising. Advertisements are served by
        a third party and are not under the site's control. Advertisements are
        labelled and separated from the site's own content. No advertiser
        pays for a page, a placement, a placement in a search result, or a
        mention of a product in a guide.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of the site</h2>
      <p>
        The site is published for personal use. You may read it, print it and
        link to it. You may not republish substantial parts of the guides as
        your own work, or use the calculators to build a product that competes
        with the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may change as the site changes. The review date below is
        the date this text was last read.
      </p>
      <p class="muted-block">Last reviewed: 20 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
